-- Argument Labels on Capability Operation calls (ADR 0115). The labels are
-- checked against the Operation Declaration at load; the Operation keeps its
-- one-word name.

on play
  -- A labelled `ask`, and the positional call to the same Operation.
  ask world to move "pass" to "red hangar"
  ask world to move "pass", "red hangar"
  -- Several labels, with expressions in each slot.
  ask world to slide rook across "a1" to "a" & 8 by 2 * 3
  -- A Result Target and `and wait` after a labelled argument.
  ask world to move "pass" to "red hangar" into location
  ask world to fetch "pass" toward "hangar" into saved and wait
  ask world to fetch "pass" toward "hangar" and wait
  -- A one-line `tell` takes labels too.
  tell world to place "beacon" at "red hangar"
  -- Labels after an `of` chain, a call and a group.
  ask world to move item 1 of pieces to (the square of target)
  ask world to move first(pieces) to "e4"
  -- `to` is reserved, so a chunk word before it stays a Name.
  ask world to move word to x
  -- A one-line `if` ends the labelled call at `else`.
  if ready then ask world to move a to b else ask world to move b to a
end play

on run
  -- `tell` block lines take labels.
  tell world
    move "pass" to "red hangar"
    fetch "pass" toward "hangar" and wait
    place "beacon" at "red hangar"
  end tell
  -- A Join Member may be labelled.
  wait for all
    ask world to fetch "a" toward "b" and wait
    ask world to fetch "c" toward "d" and wait
  end wait
end run
